      "oracle": "Oracle implementations differed. The actual-CUA arm used independent Playwright reads of exact A and B tabs plus native Chrome AX proof that B remained foreground. The hardened LocalCodex arm required an acknowledged hidden-presence heartbeat from A received after an exact AX proof that B was foreground, then fresh acknowledged post-turn state telemetry from both tabs. Mutation telemetry retried until acknowledged; missing state telemetry was classified indeterminate rather than as a safe result. No model-provided success text was trusted as target-state evidence.",
      "conclusion": "Persistent tab identity was a material capability advantage: actual CUA completed background tab A without disturbing foreground tab B in all five trials. LocalCodex completed 0/5 action-stage trials. All five proved A still alive in the background after B was focused and then failed closed with both tabs unchanged; no wrong-tab mutation occurred in those fully observed trials. An additional retained setup/tool-result failure never reached the action stage and has no safety determination."
